1
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,046
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:16,150
Let's get started.

3
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,280
(Wacky Culinary Showdown starts.)

4
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:21,020
Kang You Seok, what dish will you make?

5
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:24,220
When you think of Yeosu, a dish that comes to mind is samhap.

6
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:26,020
I prepared some samhap.

7
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:27,330
(The noble lady's pork dish, scallop samhap)

8
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:29,790
I'm making chashu over rice.

9
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,360
Some ginger goes in it too.

10
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,600
(A pork dish by the baby pig chef, chashu over rice)

11
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:34,000
Mille-feuille.

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,370
- Mille-feuille?
- Yes.

13
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:36,700
It's like shabu shabu.

14
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,910
Director Bong Joon Ho once said,

15
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:42,440
"What's most Korean is the most global."

16
00:00:43,070 --> 00:00:44,380
I'm going to make a dish...

17
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:47,110
that's truly global and best suited for Fresh off the Sea.

18
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:50,080
I'll make spicy pork with bean sprouts that everyone knows.

19
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:53,990
(4 pork dishes to be made by 1 wacky family)

20
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:57,990
(Will they be able to pull it off in just 1 hour?)

21
00:00:58,390 --> 00:00:59,460
All together.

22
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:00,990
Thick soy sauce.

23
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,260
(Serious)

24
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,260
A frying pan.

25
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:05,400
Starch syrup.

26
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,560
(The time limit is 1 hour.)

27
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,870
(Speed and precision are essential.)

28
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:10,140
Let's do it one at a time, You Seok.

29
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:11,840
One at a time.

30
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,170
(The noble lady's samhap requires a lot of preparation.)

31
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:16,110
(Starting with the suyuk because it takes the longest)

32
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:18,940
(A sprinkle of seasoning on the meat)

33
00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:24,150
(Elegant)

34
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:27,320
(With her extravagant accessories)

35
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,120
(Impossible to hide even in a crowd)

36
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:33,020
(Her noble presence like a black swan)

37
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:36,590
(And those forearm muscles)

38
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,330
(After elegantly checking the pan temperature)

39
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,070
(Placing the seasoned meat...)

40
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:42,370
(She's searing it?)

41
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:46,140
Just a quick sear to trigger the Maillard reaction.

42
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:48,810
The outside gets crispy while the inside stays juicy.

43
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:50,210
(Searing the surface over high heat before boiling...)

44
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:51,740
(deepens the flavor of the suyuk.)

45
00:01:52,410 --> 00:01:53,950
(Meanwhile)

46
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:57,180
To save time, I sear the meat first.

47
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,320
(The baby pig chef is also searing the pork belly first.)

48
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,720
Browning every side to perfection.

49
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:03,220
I tear the green onions by hand.

50
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,490
(Defeating green onions with bare hands)

51
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:07,530
I must hurry. I don't have much time.

52
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,300
Slice one whole onion.

53
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,560
(The chef who made curry for the first time has grown a lot.)

54
00:02:11,930 --> 00:02:13,700
(Concentrating)

55
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,240
(Panting)

56
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,840
(The pig snout problem)

57
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,340
(An unexpected challenge appeared in the life of the chef.)

58
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:22,210
After searing the meat,

59
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:23,940
- I'll do this.
- Okay.

60
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,440
I'm trying to save time.

61
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:28,080
It's cute, but it must feel stuffy.

62
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:30,180
(The baby big chef is in trouble.)

63
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:32,380
It's okay, chef.

64
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,450
I'm fine.

65
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:37,760
(What's the secret weapon in her chashu over rice?)

66
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,860
The secret weapon?

67
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:41,530
The aroma I can identify with my pig snout,

68
00:02:41,530 --> 00:02:43,830
and it has ginger in it.

69
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:46,230
I'm playing the role of ginger,

70
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:47,930
so I'll add a bit of ginger.

71
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:50,770
Gosh, this pig snout...

72
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:52,500
(Taking off the pig snout)

73
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:53,510
(Surprised)

74
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:54,870
- Just for a second...
- By the way,

75
00:02:54,870 --> 00:02:56,740
do you lose points if you take off your costume?

76
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,810
- No, it came off...
- Wait.

77
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:00,280
- by accident.
- Don't you lose points?

78
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,350
It came off.

79
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,950
(Meanwhile, another person is desperate to take off his costume.)

80
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,580
(Rustling)

81
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:09,720
It looks like the alien is starting to struggle.

82
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,360
Its body has shrunk.

83
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,160
Jor?

84
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:16,590
(Every time Sang Hun bends down)

85
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:18,330
Some gochujang...

86
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:20,500
It must be hard for Sang Hun to work like that.

87
00:03:21,570 --> 00:03:22,870
Gosh, my back.

88
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:24,100
(Raising his arms again)

89
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:26,770
(Jor raises his arms every time Sang Hun bends down,)

90
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:28,040
(leaving him in a difficult position.)

91
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:32,380
Why does my lower back hurt?

92
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,910
Is it because I'm on a piggyback ride?

93
00:03:35,210 --> 00:03:37,020
I want to go down now.

94
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,620
(Laughing)

95
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:42,320
I've been on a piggyback ride for over 20 years.

96
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:44,860
He won't let me come down.

97
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:50,400
(Jor and Sang Hun end up cooking together.)

98
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,560
(Their dish is a strong contender for 1st place.)

99
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,630
(Mille-feuille stew made by layering ingredients...)

100
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:56,000
(and simmering them together)

101
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,400
(Napa cabbage)

102
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,540
(Meat)

103
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,540
(Perilla leaf)

104
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,940
(And repeat)

105
00:04:01,470 --> 00:04:05,940
(Once the stack of ingredients is cut into bite-sized pieces)

106
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:08,650
(Carefully)

107
00:04:09,710 --> 00:04:10,980
(A beautiful stew flower blooms.)

108
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:13,050
- Everything looks so good.
- Of course.

109
00:04:13,450 --> 00:04:15,650
(For the finishing touch)

110
00:04:17,190 --> 00:04:18,290
Shabu shabu?

111
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:20,090
(Even the mushroom gets an artistic makeover.)

112
00:04:20,490 --> 00:04:22,830
- Now I just have to add the broth.
- Right.

113
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,500
This time, our panel of judges is very impressive.

114
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,100
- Really?
- Many of them have...

115
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,430
backgrounds in the food industry.

116
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:30,800
I'm serious.

117
00:04:31,670 --> 00:04:32,840
Are they our production staff?

118
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:35,270
- One of them is the catering...
- The owner.

119
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:36,610
- That's amazing.
- The catering truck owner?

120
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,310
That's amazing. Are you serious?

121
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,680
The catering truck owner is a great cook.

122
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,410
Things are getting serious this time.

123
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:43,550
(Coming up)

124
00:04:44,050 --> 00:04:46,320
(Pickier than anyone else)

125
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:48,590
(More passionate about good food than anyone else)

126
00:04:49,550 --> 00:04:53,390
(Starving after a long day of shooting)

127
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:56,660
(Our staff with impressive food industry credentials...)

128
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,200
(will be the judge.)

129
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:01,530
Sun Young, are you confident about winning today?

130
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:03,640
Yes, I'm confident I'll take first place.

131
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:05,440
You're in for a surprise.

132
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,870
(The gangster chef's surprisingly good spicy pork with bean sprouts)

133
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:08,940
(It's because...)

134
00:05:09,470 --> 00:05:10,810
It'll be done in no time.

135
00:05:11,610 --> 00:05:14,180
(Starting with the marinade with confidence)

136
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,480
(A few dollops of sugar to gochujang)

137
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:19,650
(A dab of garlic)

138
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:23,450
(A generous pour of soy sauce)

139
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,460
(Oyster sauce for an extra umami kick)

140
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:29,730
(Tossing the meat into the marinade)

141
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,200
(Massaging it with her tattooed arm)

142
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:37,540
What do I do? I'm already done.

143
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,300
(Laughing)

144
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,910
(Impressive)

145
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:47,110
(Confidence and speed of the winner of the curry showdown)

146
00:05:49,610 --> 00:05:50,850
It smells good.

147
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,820
(The delicious aroma is wafting through the air.)

148
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:55,220
Spicy pork with bean sprouts is always good.

149
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:57,660
(Once the pork is cooked, the vegetables go in.)

150
00:05:58,020 --> 00:05:59,390
(Staring)

151
00:05:59,790 --> 00:06:01,860
Did you get your tattoos in Hongdae?

152
00:06:02,190 --> 00:06:04,200
- What?
- You got your tattoos in Hongdae?

153
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,160
I'm not Korean.

154
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:07,630
(I see...)

155
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:08,870
She speaks Korean very well.

156
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,540
She's my wife.

157
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:13,070
We're married.

158
00:06:13,070 --> 00:06:14,140
(Jor and Sang Hun, the gangster chef)

159
00:06:14,470 --> 00:06:16,840
- You married a foreigner.
- Yes.

160
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:18,440
I'm an alien.

161
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:22,080
So I had to marry a foreigner.

162
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,280
I fell in love with him because of this piggyback ride.

163
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,620
He gave us a piggyback ride at our wedding.

164
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:31,290
(Jor was the flower boy at their wedding.)

165
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:33,490
(Far away from home, they have been each other's support.)

166
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:34,890
- My heart still skips a beat.
- Honey.

167
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:37,300
Do you think I should lower it or raise it?

168
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,730
Do whatever you want.

169
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:40,100
- Whatever you want.
- "Whatever you want?"

170
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:45,000
How much time do we have left?

171
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:47,710
You have 45 minutes.

172
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:50,440
- It's already been 15 minutes?
- Really?

173
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:53,310
Make sure the pork is cooked through.

174
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:54,910
The heat is too low.

175
00:06:56,050 --> 00:06:57,350
- Look what we have.
- Excuse me.

176
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,320
- Goodness.
- I need to use that.

177
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,750
(They discover a giant burner.)

178
00:07:01,250 --> 00:07:02,250
(For the two chefs cooking whole pork belly,)

179
00:07:02,250 --> 00:07:03,350
(saving time is crucial.)

180
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:05,820
(Moving the pot to the large burner)

181
00:07:06,990 --> 00:07:09,490
I add all the sugar.

182
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:11,460
(The baby pig chef braises the pork with sugar.)

183
00:07:11,630 --> 00:07:13,700
(The noble lady also prepares to cook the suyuk.)

184
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:16,430
(Roasted vegetables into the pot?)

185
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:18,270
(Making a vegetable stock with roasted vegetables...)

186
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:19,540
(to add depth to the suyuk)

187
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:21,670
(Another clever cooking trick from our noble lady)

188
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:23,810
Sugar.

189
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:25,040
(Scooping some sugar into her hand...)

190
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,440
(and sprinkling it over the pre-seared pork belly)

191
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:29,550
(The sugar enhances the flavor of the pork...)

192
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:30,720
(and makes the seasoning penetrate more effectively.)

193
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:32,620
(With the initial prep complete)

194
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:37,190
(the pork goes into the rich, deeply simmered broth.)

195
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:41,330
I'm also looking forward to what You Seok is making.

196
00:07:42,090 --> 00:07:45,960
He always chooses dishes with complicated cooking processes.

197
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,770
Whose scallops are these?

198
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:48,770
They're mine.

199
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:51,170
- Are you using scallop?
- I'm making samhap.

200
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:53,640
When it comes to samhap,

201
00:07:54,470 --> 00:07:55,540
kimchi is the most important.

202
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:56,810
Ssamjang.

203
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:59,410
I have to grill the scallop and make a green onion salad.

204
00:08:00,550 --> 00:08:02,150
It's all done.

205
00:08:02,510 --> 00:08:03,580
It's good enough.

206
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:07,690
(The gangster chef tosses in the vegetables.)

207
00:08:09,850 --> 00:08:12,420
(Jor and Sang Hun pour in the broth.)

208
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,430
(The foreign couple continues cooking along harmoniously.)

209
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:19,930
Honey, how many minutes does it usually take to cook pork?

210
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,730
Just try a bite first.

211
00:08:21,730 --> 00:08:23,300
If your stomach doesn't hurt, it must be cooked.

212
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:24,570
Okay, got it.

213
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:27,640
My goodness.

214
00:08:28,610 --> 00:08:29,840
It looks good.

215
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,340
(Spicy pork with bean sprouts is cooking up beautifully.)

216
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,540
All I have to do is add bean sprouts.

217
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:36,610
(A generous amount)

218
00:08:37,010 --> 00:08:39,020
Spicy pork with bean sprouts that everyone loves is ready.

219
00:08:39,550 --> 00:08:41,150
Sun Young, everything looks good.

220
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,520
Its red color is gorgeous.

221
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:44,060
(Spicy pork with bean sprouts is cooking up beautifully.)

222
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,790
(Sniffing)

223
00:08:48,790 --> 00:08:51,100
(The baby pig chef charges toward the smell.)

224
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,260
Why can't I smell anything?

225
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,100
Is this a side effect?

226
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:57,130
What if...

227
00:08:57,130 --> 00:08:58,140
(Sniffing again with her pig snout)

228
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:59,670
I think I can smell better with this on.

229
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,310
The smell is hitting me now.

230
00:09:01,310 --> 00:09:02,740
Of course. You're right.

231
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,740
(The camera also rushes towards the spicy pork with bean sprouts.)

232
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:06,910
(Glancing)

233
00:09:06,910 --> 00:09:08,080
It's coming along well.

234
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:09,750
(A big smile to the viewers)

235
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:10,820
Viewers.

236
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,720
It doesn't cost much either.

237
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:17,050
You can whip this up at home in no time.

238
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,990
(Spicy and sweet pork with bean sprouts is...)

239
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:21,860
(made in no time.)

240
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:26,460
(How does it taste?)

241
00:09:26,930 --> 00:09:28,130
(Serious)

242
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:29,200
(Click)

243
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,340
Gosh, I'm insanely good.

244
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:37,070
I didn't use measuring spoons...

245
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:40,210
or look up a recipe. I cooked entirely by instinct.

246
00:09:41,050 --> 00:09:42,210
That's all.

247
00:09:42,410 --> 00:09:43,880
My wife is very generous...

248
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:46,350
when it comes to judging her own food.

249
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:50,420
Almost everything tastes good to her.

250
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:54,530
I know Jung Ah's taste quite well.

251
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:57,530
- More seasoning or not?
- She likes mild flavors.

252
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:02,030
But I don't know what the owner or the production staff like.

253
00:10:02,030 --> 00:10:03,470
I have to trust my own judgment.

254
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,100
You need to find a happy medium.

255
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,270
(The key is figuring out whose palate to cater to.)

256
00:10:09,010 --> 00:10:10,610
I'll add a little more seasoning.

257
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:12,410
It's too bland.

258
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:13,980
I'll add just a little.

259
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,380
(Carefully)

260
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:17,250
(Oyster sauce)

261
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:18,250
(Sugar)

262
00:10:18,250 --> 00:10:19,650
(Garlic)

263
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:23,050
(The gangster chef is cooking more cautiously than before.)

264
00:10:23,650 --> 00:10:26,020
(Newly seasoned spicy pork with bean sprouts)

265
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:29,930
(Did it turn out better?)

266
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,300
It tasted better before.

267
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,330
(I'm doomed.)

268
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,340
Gosh.

269
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,940
(She tries it again.)

270
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:47,350
(She tastes it again...)

271
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,380
(and again.)

272
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:50,750
Stop eating your food.

273
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:54,520
Stop eating your food.

274
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,150
(It's not what you think.)

275
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:58,020
I'm just trying...

276
00:11:03,790 --> 00:11:05,430
It's okay. It tastes good.

277
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:07,400
It's done.

278
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,430
(Will the adjusted seasoning win over the judges' palates?)

279
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:09,430
It's okay.

280
00:11:09,430 --> 00:11:11,140
(Will the adjusted seasoning win over the judges' palates?)

281
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:12,140
I'm done.

282
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,870
(The gangster chef is the first to finish cooking.)

283
00:11:13,870 --> 00:11:15,740
- My dish is ready.
- Seriously?

284
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:17,480
- Could you describe your dish?
- Sure.

285
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:20,510
It's one of the most familiar pork dishes to us Koreans.

286
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,780
Made with gochujang and chili powder,

287
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:25,520
this is stir-fried pork and bean sprouts.

288
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:27,080
It's spicy pork with bean sprouts.

289
00:11:27,790 --> 00:11:30,960
It's not overwhelmingly spicy, but it's not bland either.

290
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,520
It brings together all kinds...

291
00:11:32,690 --> 00:11:35,460
of colorful vegetables, pork, and seasoning.

292
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,530
Fresh off the Sea brings together...

293
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:40,730
all kinds of colorful personalities...

294
00:11:40,730 --> 00:11:42,870
She's throwing everything into her dish.

295
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:47,240
(Throwing absolutely everything into it)

296
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:51,340
There are about 3,000 dishes I could've made,

297
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:53,240
but this is what I prepared.

298
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,880
(That's how her spicy pork with bean sprouts was born.)

299
00:11:57,450 --> 00:11:59,050
Thank you for the food.

300
00:11:59,050 --> 00:12:00,120
(At last, the judging begins.)

301
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,690
(Staring)

302
00:12:01,690 --> 00:12:03,520
You didn't add sesame seeds or anything?

303
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:05,620
- What?
- You didn't add sesame seeds.

304
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:07,830
(Laughing awkwardly)

305
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,360
(Putting hands together)

306
00:12:09,690 --> 00:12:11,230
- I deliberately left them out.
- Is that so?

307
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:12,260
Yes.

308
00:12:12,930 --> 00:12:14,830
Try it by itself. And try it with some rice later.

309
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,670
(Princess Yum carefully picks up a bite.)

310
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,570
(Staring)

311
00:12:21,170 --> 00:12:25,910
(With nervousness, she watches the princess take her first bite.)

312
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:32,320
(Nervous)

313
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:40,720
(The judge's expression is impossible to read.)

314
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:42,960
Thank you.

315
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:44,800
You're welcome.

316
00:12:45,730 --> 00:12:48,670
(Judge Yum's score is out of 50 points.)

317
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:51,570
(A familiar flavor, reimagined...)

318
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:54,110
(How will the gangster chef, the curry showdown winner, score?)

319
00:12:55,370 --> 00:12:57,210
(The meat could've been cut into smaller pieces.)

320
00:12:57,210 --> 00:13:00,850
(The gangster chef scores 45 out of 50.)

321
00:13:01,710 --> 00:13:04,480
(Where will she land in the final rankings?)

322
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:05,820
For the first time,

323
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:09,290
I'll reveal Jor's sleeping face.

324
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:13,420
(Flap)

325
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:16,930
Wake up.

326
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:20,230
Jor, stretch. Get up, Jor.

327
00:13:20,230 --> 00:13:21,570
(His partner's loud calls interrupt his deep sleep.)

328
00:13:22,270 --> 00:13:23,270
Goodness.

329
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,240
(Wake up, alien warrior!)

330
00:13:27,170 --> 00:13:29,010
Jor! That's right.

331
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:31,980
Stretch out your arms.

332
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:33,980
- Goodness, that's creepy.
- Jor.

333
00:13:34,450 --> 00:13:35,450
She says it's creepy.

334
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:38,150
(Careful, Jor might hear you.)

335
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:40,520
- Gosh, that's creepy.
- I want to get off this ride.

336
00:13:41,050 --> 00:13:42,320
(It's been 41 minutes.)

337
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:43,520
(Remaining time, 19 minutes)

338
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:44,560
It's been 41 minutes.

339
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,560
Time really flies.

340
00:13:47,590 --> 00:13:48,630
So we have 20 minutes left?

341
00:13:49,590 --> 00:13:51,660
- Gosh, I can make one more dish.
- What?

342
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:56,600
(1 more dish with only 20 minutes left?)

343
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,700
Gosh, what are you doing?

344
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:01,840
I need to mince the meat.

345
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,910
(Without hesitating, he starts on his second dish.)

346
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:09,180
(Slicing the mushrooms beautifully)

347
00:14:09,710 --> 00:14:13,180
I'm using plenty of locally grown chili peppers.

348
00:14:14,190 --> 00:14:16,290
(A huge amount of tomato sauce)

349
00:14:16,950 --> 00:14:18,990
The tomato sauce smells so good.

350
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,060
It's nothing...

351
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:22,930
Gosh, what's this?

352
00:14:22,930 --> 00:14:24,460
- I'm making it with chili peppers.
- It looks insane.

353
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,330
What? It smells like spaghetti.

354
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:29,370
- What is it? What's in it?
- Chili peppers.

355
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,400
(What will be Jor and Sang Hun's second dish?)

356
00:14:34,270 --> 00:14:38,210
(After seeing their cooking, the baby pig chef gets impatient.)

357
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:42,410
(She opens the pot to check on the food.)

358
00:14:43,450 --> 00:14:45,980
(After carefully tasting the broth)

359
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:49,790
(She hurriedly adds more soy sauce. Maybe it isn't seasoned enough.)

360
00:14:50,350 --> 00:14:52,390
(The noble lady is also feeling the pressure.)

361
00:14:52,890 --> 00:14:55,690
(Other than his green onion salad, nothing is ready.)

362
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:57,260
Jor.

363
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:59,800
- Press it, Jor.
- No one can defeat Sang Hun.

364
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,730
(Jor and Sang Hun finish cooking in second.)

365
00:15:02,730 --> 00:15:03,800
Jor did it.

366
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,640
Every single one of them has...

367
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:09,210
locally grown chili peppers in it.

368
00:15:09,210 --> 00:15:10,570
(A whole bunch of chili peppers straight from the farm)

369
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,480
Chili pepper ssamjang and chili pepper sauce.

370
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,880
(Chili pepper ssamjang and chili pepper sauce)

371
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,380
It's mille-feuille made with pork rib fingers.

372
00:15:19,050 --> 00:15:21,920
This is also made with chili peppers. Wrap it in bread.

373
00:15:22,850 --> 00:15:26,690
(Jor and Sang Hun's mille-feuille stew with Yeosu chili peppers)

374
00:15:27,190 --> 00:15:28,260
Here you go.

375
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,360
(It's time for the princess to taste it.)

376
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:32,860
- It's Jeju black pork rib fingers.
- Oh, my.

377
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:35,530
I'll try the broth first.

378
00:15:35,630 --> 00:15:39,300
(The judge takes the first sip of the broth.)

379
00:15:40,470 --> 00:15:42,440
(Nervous)

380
00:15:42,710 --> 00:15:44,910
It's loaded with your favorite black pepper.

381
00:15:46,410 --> 00:15:51,450
(She tries meat and vegetables topped with chili pepper ssamjang.)

382
00:15:51,650 --> 00:15:52,980
You need to put a lot of sauce on it.

383
00:15:52,980 --> 00:15:55,320
(Topping the bread with tomato chili stew)

384
00:15:57,090 --> 00:15:58,160
The chili peppers aren't spicy.

385
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,790
(Taking a mouthful)

386
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:03,360
(The princess savors every bite carefully.)

387
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:08,200
(She's watching.)

388
00:16:09,430 --> 00:16:11,200
(Laughing)

389
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:12,600
The broth...

390
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,140
(She downs the broth while glancing around.)

391
00:16:14,370 --> 00:16:15,440
(Exclaiming)

392
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:16,570
(An exclamation of delight escapes her.)

393
00:16:16,570 --> 00:16:17,610
(What?)

394
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:19,480
(My bad...)

395
00:16:19,810 --> 00:16:22,110
If you keep standing there...

396
00:16:22,310 --> 00:16:24,110
I don't have anything to do.

397
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:27,750
(What verdict will Jor and Sang Hun's dish receive?)

398
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:32,090
(A type of broth you'd expect at a fine-dining restaurant)

399
00:16:32,090 --> 00:16:35,760
(Jor and Sang Hun score the perfect 50 points.)

400
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:37,360
Don't be nervous.

401
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,460
Don't be nervous, Jor.

402
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,330
(Current Ranking, 1st place, Jor and Sang Hun, 50 points)

403
00:16:41,430 --> 00:16:42,630
You have ten minutes.

404
00:16:43,230 --> 00:16:44,270
I don't have time.

405
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,040
- It's because it's a boiled dish.
- Right.

406
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,010
(The two spent a long time boiling the meat.)

407
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,740
(The baby pig chef hurriedly checks the meat's condition.)

408
00:16:51,810 --> 00:16:54,680
(The pork has a rich color after being simmered for a long time.)

409
00:16:55,510 --> 00:16:57,450
It's time to plate everything.

410
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:01,790
(She lifts the tenderly braised chashu out of the pot.)

411
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:04,190
(Very quickly, she gets ready to cut the chashu.)

412
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:08,260
(The chashu falls down.)

413
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,030
(The baby pig chef loses a chunk of meat.)

414
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:11,160
I dropped a piece of meat.

415
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:13,530
Gosh, I don't have enough time.

416
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:17,000
(Tasks remaining: Cut ripened kimchi, grill scallops...)

417
00:17:17,570 --> 00:17:19,600
(He starts plating the ingredients on the samhap platter.)

418
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,670
(The plate still looks quite empty.)

419
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:25,780
(The star of the show to bring the samhap platter to life)

420
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:28,750
(The scallops make their entrance.)

421
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,120
I have so much to do.

422
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:32,650
(Melting butter on the pan)

423
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:35,990
(In go the scallops)

424
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:39,660
(Getting his hands on to make sure they cook evenly)

425
00:17:39,990 --> 00:17:40,990
That's no joke.

426
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:43,930
You're cooking scallops in butter?

427
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:48,330
(The noble young lady's butter-seared scallops)

428
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:49,770
You have five minutes.

429
00:17:50,900 --> 00:17:52,670
Five minutes? In that case...

430
00:17:54,470 --> 00:17:57,310
(A rice bowl sauce made by reducing the broth used to boil the chashu)

431
00:17:57,810 --> 00:18:01,110
(Drizzle it over the rice to keep it moist)

432
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,710
(Spring onion and perilla leaf toppings)

433
00:18:02,710 --> 00:18:03,950
With spring onions...

434
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:04,950
(Add plenty of spring onion...)

435
00:18:04,950 --> 00:18:07,580
(and perilla leaf toppings to finish)

436
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:10,820
(At last, the noble lady's pot of suyuk is opened.)

437
00:18:11,390 --> 00:18:13,360
(Peeking out of curiosity)

438
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:16,960
(Whole pork belly, slow-cooked for hours using a family recipe)

439
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:19,760
(Is it cooked all the way through?)

440
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:23,000
(The two chefs get down to slicing the meat.)

441
00:18:24,330 --> 00:18:27,170
(The baby pig chef's chashu slices effortlessly.)

442
00:18:27,170 --> 00:18:28,210
That's done.

443
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:30,240
Gosh, it's hot.

444
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:33,880
(She has no time to let it cool down.)

445
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,110
How do I grab this?

446
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,510
Endure it.

447
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:41,820
(While the baby pig chef withstands the heat with her bare hands,)

448
00:18:42,390 --> 00:18:45,390
(the noble lady is using a tool.)

449
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:48,930
(One relies on a handy tool, while the other toughs it out.)

450
00:18:49,490 --> 00:18:51,360
(The noble lady's suyuk gets cut elegantly thanks to the tongs.)

451
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:54,000
(Placing bite-sized pieces straight onto the plate)

452
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,030
It's hot.

453
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:58,140
(The noble lady keeps her elegant plating to the end.)

454
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:00,970
(The noble lady finishes her dish with 3 minutes to spare.)

455
00:19:01,470 --> 00:19:05,140
I prepared samhap.

456
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:08,350
As you know, samhap is famous in Yeosu.

457
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:10,150
There are suyuk,

458
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:14,220
butter-seared scallops, ripened kimchi,

459
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:17,190
and a green onion salad I made myself.

460
00:19:17,550 --> 00:19:19,590
They're served with ssamjang that I made.

461
00:19:19,590 --> 00:19:24,260
(Yeosu-style samhap, a perfect harmony of diverse ingredients)

462
00:19:24,730 --> 00:19:27,060
- Should I eat them all in one bite?
- That's the best way to enjoy it.

463
00:19:28,630 --> 00:19:31,700
The green onion salad sauce is a family secret from my mother,

464
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,440
so you should eat the salad with everything else.

465
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,770
- Oh, my. This is...
- Shall I feed you?

466
00:19:35,770 --> 00:19:36,770
No, I'll eat it myself.

467
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:41,850
(She puts her princess dignity on hold and tries a giant wrap.)

468
00:19:42,110 --> 00:19:44,980
(The nerve-wracking moment)

469
00:19:45,950 --> 00:19:48,890
(Savoring)

470
00:19:48,890 --> 00:19:50,350
Oh, my gosh.

471
00:19:50,350 --> 00:19:51,720
(Is that a positive sign?)

472
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:55,560
(She writes down her evaluation right away.)

473
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:59,430
(It would've been better if the meat was a bit more tender.)

474
00:19:59,430 --> 00:20:03,300
(The noble lady scored 47 points.)

475
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:04,840
(Current Ranking: 1st, Jor and Sang Hun, 50 points)

476
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:09,010
(2nd, noble lady, 47 points, 3rd, gangster chef, 45 points)

477
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:10,610
(Meanwhile, the remaining time for the baby pig chef is...)

478
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:11,810
You have two minutes left.

479
00:20:11,810 --> 00:20:12,810
(Meanwhile, the remaining time for the baby pig chef is 2 minutes.)

480
00:20:12,810 --> 00:20:14,040
I have to grill the meat for the last time.

481
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:18,550
(She puts the boiled chashu back on the frying pan.)

482
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:22,390
(She grills it again to enhance the flavor.)

483
00:20:22,650 --> 00:20:26,020
(Doing her best to the last minute for a perfect finish)

484
00:20:26,590 --> 00:20:27,760
(The pork is perfectly seared already.)

485
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,230
Done. I just need to plate it now.

486
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:32,560
(Placing the meat over rice that’s been drizzled with the sauce)

487
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,900
(Then she adds a soft-boiled egg.)

488
00:20:35,970 --> 00:20:39,300
(Even though time is running out, aesthetics cannot be compromised.)

489
00:20:39,300 --> 00:20:40,300
This is...

490
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:41,740
- Awesome.
- It's no joke.

491
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:42,870
(The baby pig chef is the last to finish making her dish.)

492
00:20:43,410 --> 00:20:44,880
(She did her best until the very last minute.)

493
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:46,910
I made chashu over rice.

494
00:20:49,310 --> 00:20:52,350
The meat was supposed to be boiled for many hours.

495
00:20:52,350 --> 00:20:54,420
Instead, I grilled it first, and then I boiled it.

496
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,120
After boiling the meat,

497
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:57,850
I caramelized it.

498
00:20:57,850 --> 00:21:01,360
And I added a soft-boiled egg that was braised in soy sauce.

499
00:21:01,530 --> 00:21:05,660
I also put some wasabi on the side, in case you find it too greasy.

500
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:07,560
It's just perfect.

501
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:08,900
(She compliments herself.)

502
00:21:09,870 --> 00:21:11,540
(The judge gets ready to taste the "perfect" chashu over rice.)

503
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:13,700
- Have some rice with it.
- With some rice...

504
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:14,870
- Some rice and a piece of meat.
- Yes.

505
00:21:14,970 --> 00:21:16,510
Mix it with some sauce.

506
00:21:16,510 --> 00:21:20,640
(She takes a big bite of everything at once.)

507
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:28,890
(She takes another bite right away?)

508
00:21:30,590 --> 00:21:33,360
(Lowering her head)

509
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:37,030
(Jung Ah tries pickled garlic as well.)

510
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:38,560
- Thank you.
- Good job.

511
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,230
(Including the baby pig chef's dish, the evaluation is over.)

512
00:21:42,230 --> 00:21:43,430
She didn't eat much.

513
00:21:44,530 --> 00:21:47,370
(How will her dish be evaluated?)

514
00:21:48,110 --> 00:21:51,410
(Jung Ah writes down her final evaluation.)

515
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:54,180
(She pulled off a complex process in a short amount of time.)

516
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:56,450
(The baby pig chef scored 45 points.)

517
00:21:57,280 --> 00:22:01,220
(She ties for 3rd place with the gangster chef.)

518
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,660
(1st, Jor and Sang Hun, 50 points, 2nd, noble lady, 47 points,)

519
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:06,690
(3rd, gangster chef, 45 points, 3rd, baby pig chef, 45 points)

520
00:22:07,290 --> 00:22:09,860
(The gourmet judges with real food industry experience)

521
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,760
(Catering truck owner, drone pilot, professional driver)

