My goodness.

776
00:32:26,884 --> 00:32:27,954
I can't believe this.

777
00:32:28,214 --> 00:32:29,224
(Screaming with joy?)

778
00:32:29,484 --> 00:32:30,724
Oh, I'm not the winner.

779
00:32:31,784 --> 00:32:32,824
I knew it.

780
00:32:32,824 --> 00:32:33,824
- My goodness.
- I'm in last place.

781
00:32:33,824 --> 00:32:35,524
See? I told you I was in last place.

782
00:32:35,524 --> 00:32:36,564
- What was that?
- This is amazing.

783
00:32:36,564 --> 00:32:37,864
(Disheartened)

784
00:32:37,864 --> 00:32:39,134
(Gangster chef: Jung Ah, 45, gourmet judges, 40.7, total, 85.7)

785
00:32:39,864 --> 00:32:40,894
Oh, my.

786
00:32:41,594 --> 00:32:42,704
Thank you so much.

787
00:32:43,064 --> 00:32:44,734
- I'm impressed, You Seok.
- Honestly...

788
00:32:44,734 --> 00:32:46,974
- He's improved a lot.
- I couldn't even imagine this.

789
00:32:47,334 --> 00:32:48,334
(Impressed)

790
00:32:48,334 --> 00:32:49,444
I'm serious.

791
00:32:49,874 --> 00:32:52,074
Really? But I understand why he won the contest.

792
00:32:52,074 --> 00:32:53,774
I was so surprised when I first tasted his dish.

793
00:32:53,774 --> 00:32:56,414
It would've been much better if I had had just ten more minutes.

794
00:32:57,414 --> 00:32:59,084
"The ultimate, foolproof combination."

795
00:32:59,084 --> 00:33:00,184
"The ultimate, foolproof combination?"

796
00:33:00,184 --> 00:33:01,984
- You can't go wrong with it.
- It's the ultimate combination.

797
00:33:02,724 --> 00:33:03,824
But why...

798
00:33:03,824 --> 00:33:05,554
(I can't believe I placed 1st.)

799
00:33:06,554 --> 00:33:07,554
Sun Young...

800
00:33:07,554 --> 00:33:08,624
(Laughing silently)

801
00:33:09,724 --> 00:33:12,364
(Sulky)

802
00:33:12,994 --> 00:33:15,904
(The last place was sulking while hearing the reviews of the winner.)

803
00:33:15,904 --> 00:33:16,904
(Pouting)

804
00:33:16,904 --> 00:33:18,804
(Still pouting)

805
00:33:18,974 --> 00:33:21,134
- But her dish was good too.
- They must be gourmets.

806
00:33:21,334 --> 00:33:22,474
(Giggling)

807
00:33:22,474 --> 00:33:23,974
Her spicy pork with bean sprouts was really good.

808
00:33:24,144 --> 00:33:25,174
Sun Young.

809
00:33:25,174 --> 00:33:26,714
(Sun Young, are you all right?)

810
00:33:28,074 --> 00:33:29,244
(How can you laugh right now?)

811
00:33:29,244 --> 00:33:30,484
You had your hopes up a bit, right?

812
00:33:30,644 --> 00:33:31,914
Sun Young, are you sulking?

813
00:33:32,484 --> 00:33:34,114
- You suddenly look so deflated.
- Sorry?

814
00:33:34,114 --> 00:33:35,554
(The same place, the different vibes)

815
00:33:35,654 --> 00:33:36,984
Sun Young, your dish...

816
00:33:36,984 --> 00:33:38,654
What? I don't want to hear it.

817
00:33:38,654 --> 00:33:40,554
- It tasted good, - I said, I'm good.

818
00:33:40,724 --> 00:33:42,664
but it made them want to keep drinking water.

819
00:33:43,094 --> 00:33:44,224
- It was a bit too salty?
- I see.

820
00:33:44,394 --> 00:33:45,764
You could just drink water.

821
00:33:46,164 --> 00:33:47,534
Don't we have drinking water in this country?

822
00:33:48,094 --> 00:33:51,664
Those who are on the older side can find it a bit too salty.

823
00:33:51,664 --> 00:33:54,234
I saw the look on their faces earlier.

824
00:33:55,304 --> 00:33:56,674
- But the bottom place...
- Unbelievable.

825
00:33:56,674 --> 00:33:57,974
(Was it really bad enough to come in last?)

826
00:33:58,504 --> 00:33:59,614
(You should taste it again.)

827
00:33:59,614 --> 00:34:00,644
- You should...
- Just...

828
00:34:00,644 --> 00:34:01,644
Sun Young, why...

829
00:34:02,384 --> 00:34:04,814
Her outfit makes her look so scary.

830
00:34:05,354 --> 00:34:07,554
(She's so hilarious.)

831
00:34:08,314 --> 00:34:11,124
(The eventful Wacky Culinary Showdown ended.)

832
00:34:12,124 --> 00:34:14,654
(Before Sang Hun leaves, everyone huddles up to say goodbye.)

833
00:34:14,654 --> 00:34:16,524
- Good job, everyone.
- Good job, everyone.

834
00:34:16,524 --> 00:34:17,524
I had such a great time.

835
00:34:17,524 --> 00:34:18,664
(The siblings look back on the day with a cozy chat.)

836
00:34:18,964 --> 00:34:21,394
- Please don't forget us.
- How can I forget you?

837
00:34:21,994 --> 00:34:25,234
Painting together was the most memorable part.

838
00:34:25,234 --> 00:34:27,104
- Really?
- I thought so.

839
00:34:27,104 --> 00:34:31,074
I would've been so helpless without you.

840
00:34:31,074 --> 00:34:32,114
Thank you.

841
00:34:32,744 --> 00:34:34,074
While I was still working on the killer whale,

842
00:34:34,074 --> 00:34:36,344
Sang Hun drew like four different fish.

843
00:34:36,744 --> 00:34:39,114
Otherwise, you guys are going to have a long day tomorrow.

844
00:34:39,514 --> 00:34:43,084
I did my best to wrap it up as quickly as possible.

845
00:34:43,624 --> 00:34:46,424
I feel terrible that you had to do so much work.

846
00:34:46,424 --> 00:34:47,654
Come on. Don't feel that way.

847
00:34:47,794 --> 00:34:49,724
- Your face is all red now.
- I wasn't the only one who worked.

848
00:34:49,724 --> 00:34:51,394
- You're the most tanned one here.
- Really?

849
00:34:51,994 --> 00:34:54,964
(His face is noticeably darker than when he first arrived.)

850
00:34:55,464 --> 00:34:58,204
I was focused on painting. I mean, the sun beat right down on my face.

851
00:34:58,664 --> 00:35:00,874
- You came to Yeosu for us.
- You came all the way to Yeosu.

852
00:35:00,874 --> 00:35:01,974
- Exactly.
- You arrived early in the morning.

853
00:35:01,974 --> 00:35:03,244
I can't thank you enough.

854
00:35:03,804 --> 00:35:04,844
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

855
00:35:05,144 --> 00:35:07,474
(It's time for Sang Hun to leave.)

856
00:35:07,674 --> 00:35:09,144
Sang Hun is leaving now.

857
00:35:09,144 --> 00:35:10,384
- What?
- Let's say goodbye to him.

858
00:35:10,514 --> 00:35:12,414
- Let's see him off...
- That's okay. Don't get up.

859
00:35:12,514 --> 00:35:14,114
- We should see you off.
- Okay.

860
00:35:14,114 --> 00:35:16,654
Thank you so much for everything, Sang Hun.

861
00:35:16,654 --> 00:35:18,324
- I'll get going.
- Let's take a photo together.

862
00:35:18,324 --> 00:35:19,894
- Let's take a photo together.
- Sang Hun...

863
00:35:19,894 --> 00:35:21,624
- Wait.
- One, two, three.

864
00:35:22,964 --> 00:35:25,394
(They save the memories with Sang Hun.)

865
00:35:25,834 --> 00:35:27,034
- I'll get going now.
- Thank you, Sang Hun.

866
00:35:27,034 --> 00:35:28,034
- Bye.
- Go home safely.

867
00:35:28,034 --> 00:35:29,204
- I'll go to see your musical.
- Okay.

868
00:35:29,404 --> 00:35:30,534
Bye.

869
00:35:30,534 --> 00:35:32,234
(They wave their hands until he leaves.)

870
00:35:32,234 --> 00:35:33,704
- Bye, everyone.
- Go home safely.

871
00:35:33,704 --> 00:35:34,704
- Bye.
- Goodbye.

872
00:35:34,704 --> 00:35:36,974
- Go home safely.
- Bye.

873
00:35:37,274 --> 00:35:38,874
I feel so hollow.

874
00:35:39,344 --> 00:35:40,544
- Time passed so quickly.
- Exactly.

875
00:35:41,314 --> 00:35:43,884
It's hard to believe that this is our final night together.

876
00:35:43,884 --> 00:35:45,044
- Our final night together.
- Yes.

877
00:35:46,314 --> 00:35:49,724
(The summer night with a refreshing breeze)

878
00:35:50,224 --> 00:35:53,794
(Darkness settled over the sea.)

879
00:35:54,224 --> 00:35:57,964
(The night in Yeosu deepens.)

880
00:35:59,064 --> 00:36:00,934
I'm glad we painted that mural.

881
00:36:01,364 --> 00:36:02,434
I really enjoyed doing it.

882
00:36:02,434 --> 00:36:04,204
- It feels so rewarding.
- Indeed.

883
00:36:04,964 --> 00:36:06,334
I feel like I'm going to get emotional...

884
00:36:06,734 --> 00:36:08,274
when we wrap up the mural tomorrow.

885
00:36:08,734 --> 00:36:11,374
Painting the mural and treating the locals to a meal...

886
00:36:11,374 --> 00:36:13,614
- were brilliant ideas.
- I really think so too.

887
00:36:13,914 --> 00:36:15,484
- I'm really glad we did those.
- Me too.

888
00:36:16,414 --> 00:36:18,314
- I'm really glad we did those.
- Please enjoy.

889
00:36:19,054 --> 00:36:21,914
(In Maegye Village, Hadong,)

890
00:36:22,454 --> 00:36:24,454
(the siblings cooked a meal for the village seniors.)

891
00:36:24,924 --> 00:36:27,254
I really think it will feel rewarding.

892
00:36:28,054 --> 00:36:29,124
Guys, look here.

893
00:36:29,124 --> 00:36:30,194
(Cherishing all these memories in their hearts...)

894
00:36:30,364 --> 00:36:31,994
One, two, three.

895
00:36:31,994 --> 00:36:36,434
(They capture the night with a photo.)

896
00:36:36,564 --> 00:36:38,234
- Give it to her.
- Okay.

897
00:36:38,934 --> 00:36:40,934
- This is our last drink.
- I'll lay out the bedding.

898
00:36:42,174 --> 00:36:44,244
(Jung Ah lies down first as she's tired.)

899
00:36:45,344 --> 00:36:46,714
- Shall we?
- Sorry?

900
00:36:47,114 --> 00:36:48,114
She looks cute.

901
00:36:48,884 --> 00:36:50,084
Jung Ah looks cute.

902
00:36:50,284 --> 00:36:51,284
I've been...

903
00:36:52,014 --> 00:36:55,754
happy being on the show with you, Jung Ah, and Yoon Seo.

904
00:36:56,224 --> 00:36:58,724
- You Seok.
- It's my innermost feeling.

905
00:37:00,224 --> 00:37:04,894
I was lucky to get to do this show with you two and Jung Ah.

906
00:37:05,224 --> 00:37:07,934
I really think I was lucky to get to work with all of you.

907
00:37:08,194 --> 00:37:10,204
- Our chemistry is...
- It's the best.

908
00:37:10,204 --> 00:37:11,204
Indeed.

909
00:37:11,204 --> 00:37:14,104
Let's take a photo next to Jung Ah while she's asleep.

910
00:37:14,104 --> 00:37:15,134
Let's do that.

911
00:37:15,134 --> 00:37:16,904
One, two, three.

912
00:37:16,904 --> 00:37:18,704
(They gather around Jung Ah, who's asleep,)

913
00:37:19,774 --> 00:37:22,984
(and take a group selfie.)

914
00:37:23,344 --> 00:37:26,584
(This moment will be remembered forever.)

915
00:37:27,054 --> 00:37:31,854
(Another morning dawns for the siblings.)

916
00:37:32,994 --> 00:37:36,394
(What is today's first activity?)

917
00:37:36,994 --> 00:37:38,494
We should go paint the mural.

918
00:37:39,294 --> 00:37:42,764
(Here's why the siblings are busy so early in the morning.)

919
00:37:43,804 --> 00:37:46,834
(The first thing to do this morning: Painting the mural!)

920
00:37:47,434 --> 00:37:48,904
(But the sweltering heat already feels like 35°C...)

921
00:37:48,904 --> 00:37:50,304
(first thing in the morning.)

922
00:37:51,204 --> 00:37:52,644
I'm worried.

923
00:37:54,074 --> 00:37:55,114
I can see it.

924
00:37:55,114 --> 00:37:56,984
(The mural captain is worried as always.)

925
00:37:57,314 --> 00:37:58,744
It will be really hot today.

926
00:37:58,744 --> 00:38:00,814
We should make sure to slather on the sunscreen.

927
00:38:01,614 --> 00:38:02,654
Let's go.

928
00:38:03,284 --> 00:38:04,354
Shall we get going now?

929
00:38:04,984 --> 00:38:06,454
Jung Ah, we're heading out to paint the mural.

930
00:38:06,454 --> 00:38:07,624
Okay. See you later.

931
00:38:07,794 --> 00:38:09,394
- We're off.
- Bye.

932
00:38:09,394 --> 00:38:11,394
(Captain Yum stays behind to make breakfast.)

933
00:38:11,724 --> 00:38:13,634
Don't you feel like an artist?

934
00:38:13,634 --> 00:38:15,194
Exactly. Jung Ah cooks...

935
00:38:15,194 --> 00:38:17,104
while we're painting.

936
00:38:18,004 --> 00:38:19,174
Do you want a ride, You Seok?

937
00:38:19,634 --> 00:38:20,774
- You'll give me a ride?
- Would that be okay?

938
00:38:20,774 --> 00:38:22,404
- Yes, you give him a ride.
- I'll give you a ride.

939
00:38:22,904 --> 00:38:24,444
Let's break away from the cliche.

940
00:38:25,504 --> 00:38:28,214
Why doesn't Yoon Seo give a ride to You Seok?

941
00:38:29,184 --> 00:38:30,284
(Sitting in the back)

942
00:38:30,284 --> 00:38:32,214
- That's it. That's great.
- What are you doing?

943
00:38:32,214 --> 00:38:34,414
- Sit here.
- What are you doing?

944
00:38:34,414 --> 00:38:35,624
Hold on.

945
00:38:36,084 --> 00:38:38,324
(She takes off coolly.)

946
00:38:38,324 --> 00:38:39,394
Let's go.

947
00:38:39,994 --> 00:38:41,054
Hello.

948
00:38:42,794 --> 00:38:43,864
Goodness.

949
00:38:44,794 --> 00:38:45,794
Hi.

950
00:38:47,264 --> 00:38:48,434
Hi.

951
00:38:49,604 --> 00:38:51,504
Hello.

952
00:38:51,864 --> 00:38:54,304
Hello.

953
00:38:54,304 --> 00:38:56,704
(After saying hello to everyone she passes,)

954
00:38:57,544 --> 00:38:59,844
(she arrives at the mural spot first.)

955
00:39:00,144 --> 00:39:01,144
(Taking off with You Seok behind her)

956
00:39:01,144 --> 00:39:02,344
- So...
- You steer the wheels, okay?

957
00:39:03,544 --> 00:39:04,684
- You steer the wheels.
- What's this?

958
00:39:05,214 --> 00:39:06,554
I can't see anything. You steer the wheels.

959
00:39:07,684 --> 00:39:09,284
(Oh, my)

960
00:39:10,024 --> 00:39:11,354
- You need to...
- I'm doing it.

961
00:39:11,354 --> 00:39:13,594
- I can't steer the wheels.
- Goodness.

962
00:39:13,594 --> 00:39:14,594
(Is You Seok pedaling?)

963
00:39:14,954 --> 00:39:17,024
You're doing well. It's okay.

964
00:39:17,024 --> 00:39:18,394
(Yoon Seo steers, and You Seok pedals.)

965
00:39:19,794 --> 00:39:22,734
(A new kind of bicycle where the top and bottom are different)

966
00:39:24,164 --> 00:39:25,234
(It's unclear who's giving whom a ride.)

967
00:39:25,234 --> 00:39:26,674
There's a speed bump ahead.

968
00:39:27,534 --> 00:39:28,704
There's a speed bump ahead.

969
00:39:29,244 --> 00:39:31,274
Gosh, I almost fell off.

970
00:39:32,304 --> 00:39:33,344
That's incredible.

971
00:39:33,344 --> 00:39:34,344
(Being happy-go-lucky)

972
00:39:35,844 --> 00:39:38,284
Sir.

973
00:39:41,714 --> 00:39:42,784
Let's just leave it here.

974
00:39:42,784 --> 00:39:45,624
(The younger siblings arrive at the mural site in perfect sync.)

975
00:39:45,954 --> 00:39:48,294
Yoon Seo, you drew a person.

976
00:39:48,294 --> 00:39:49,564
Of course I did.

977
00:39:49,864 --> 00:39:51,994
Yoon Seo, I really like it.

978
00:39:52,434 --> 00:39:54,594
I love the person you drew.

979
00:39:54,594 --> 00:39:55,704
(Sun Young loves the painting.)

980
00:39:55,704 --> 00:39:57,304
I haven't drawn the eyes, nose, and mouth yet.

981
00:39:57,304 --> 00:39:59,534
- Are you going to draw them?
- It's not necessary.

982
00:39:59,534 --> 00:40:01,034
I don't think so either.

983
00:40:01,034 --> 00:40:03,544
I just need to distinguish the face from the body.

984
00:40:04,174 --> 00:40:06,244
(Day 1, base coat)

985
00:40:06,444 --> 00:40:08,744
(Day 2, sketching and coloring)

986
00:40:08,914 --> 00:40:11,684
(Today, Day 3 is D-Day.)

987
00:40:11,684 --> 00:40:12,714
It's really nice.

988
00:40:12,714 --> 00:40:15,054
(Coloring the sketched design)

989
00:40:15,554 --> 00:40:16,954
Isn't this a starfish?

990
00:40:16,954 --> 00:40:17,954
- Yes.
- It's a stingray.

991
00:40:18,284 --> 00:40:19,894
- Right, it's a stingray.
- Stingray.

992
00:40:20,124 --> 00:40:21,324
I'll paint the stingray.

993
00:40:21,324 --> 00:40:22,394
(I'll paint the stingray.)

994
00:40:22,724 --> 00:40:25,364
What color should I paint the stingray?

995
00:40:26,294 --> 00:40:28,694
Should I paint the whale or the other fish? Which is easier?

996
00:40:29,204 --> 00:40:30,604
Can you paint the clam?

997
00:40:31,064 --> 00:40:32,534
There's a clam. I'll do that one.

998
00:40:33,074 --> 00:40:34,974
(Pouring)

999
00:40:34,974 --> 00:40:36,944
- What's that for?
- For the orca.

1000
00:40:37,274 --> 00:40:38,274
The orca, right?

1001
00:40:39,614 --> 00:40:42,714
(The signature feature of the siblings' mural is the orca.)

1002
00:40:43,014 --> 00:40:44,084
Can you pour it?

1003
00:40:44,214 --> 00:40:45,684
(Black paint for the orca)

1004
00:40:45,684 --> 00:40:46,754
Thank you.

1005
00:40:46,954 --> 00:40:49,254
(A bit of blue... A lot)

1006
00:40:49,254 --> 00:40:50,324
I poured too much.

1007
00:40:50,724 --> 00:40:52,324
(Gushing)

1008
00:40:53,254 --> 00:40:54,294
Should I add more black?

1009
00:40:54,594 --> 00:40:56,094
No, it might be okay.

1010
00:40:56,094 --> 00:40:57,664
(Somehow, the colors come together perfectly.)

1011
00:40:58,624 --> 00:40:59,634
It will be okay.

1012
00:40:59,634 --> 00:41:01,734
(Even a mistake turns into a masterpiece.)

1013
00:41:02,564 --> 00:41:05,204
(She picks up a large brush and contemplates for a minute.)

1014
00:41:07,534 --> 00:41:11,144
(She boldly outlines the orca's back.)

1015
00:41:12,044 --> 00:41:13,714
(Concentrating)

1016
00:41:14,244 --> 00:41:16,984
(A few confident strokes on the other side)

1017
00:41:18,844 --> 00:41:21,384
(The shape of a whale emerges in no time.)

1018
00:41:23,924 --> 00:41:27,154
(Rising star of the mural world, Painter Roh)

1019
00:41:29,624 --> 00:41:31,924
(She quickly fills in the whale's back that's as big as her body.)

1020
00:41:32,564 --> 00:41:35,334
(You Seok takes care of the orca's plump belly.)

1021
00:41:35,864 --> 00:41:39,134
(Yoon Seo paints its adorable tail.)

1022
00:41:40,734 --> 00:41:44,304
(Working together, the two bring the orca to life quickly.)

1023
00:41:45,144 --> 00:41:46,844
Gosh, it looks so cute.

1024
00:41:48,474 --> 00:41:50,314
(Looking at the whale raises her dopamine level.)

1025
00:41:50,714 --> 00:41:52,184
- Does it look cute?
- Yes.

1026
00:41:53,214 --> 00:41:55,584
So this is the belly.

1027
00:41:55,584 --> 00:41:57,054
(Even the plump belly looks cute.)

1028
00:41:58,484 --> 00:42:01,224
(Sun Young's stingray is also getting complete.)

1029
00:42:01,224 --> 00:42:02,224
I'm done.

1030
00:42:04,594 --> 00:42:06,034
- The whale is done.
- Is it done?

1031
00:42:06,864 --> 00:42:07,934
Let's go.

1032
00:42:07,934 --> 00:42:09,564
(They decide to finish in the afternoon.)

1033
00:42:09,564 --> 00:42:10,564
Seriously.

1034
00:42:11,704 --> 00:42:12,874
- It's so hot.
- It's done.

1035
00:42:14,334 --> 00:42:18,304
(A special mural they're creating together in the heart of summer)

1036
00:42:18,804 --> 00:42:21,814
(We'll get cuter this afternoon.)

1037
00:42:22,644 --> 00:42:25,854
Gosh, I'm so full. I downed it in one go.

1038
00:42:26,214 --> 00:42:27,254
Let's just go back tomorrow.

1039
00:42:27,254 --> 00:42:28,254
(The siblings' special breakfast will be revealed online.)

1040
00:42:28,614 --> 00:42:31,254
- Today is our last day.
- Yes.

1041
00:42:31,724 --> 00:42:35,124
Since you've been working hard,

1042
00:42:35,124 --> 00:42:36,594
we prepared a special gift.

1043
00:42:36,594 --> 00:42:37,764
- Really?
- Seriously?

1044
00:42:37,764 --> 00:42:38,824
(We prepared a special gift.)

1045
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:41,860
- Today is our last day.
- Yes.

1046
00:42:42,230 --> 00:42:45,630
Since you've been working hard,

1047
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:47,200
we prepared a special gift.

1048
00:42:47,200 --> 00:42:48,300
- Really?
- Seriously?

1049
00:42:48,300 --> 00:42:49,840
(We prepared a special gift.)

1050
00:42:50,340 --> 00:42:51,540
(Seriously?)

1051
00:42:51,540 --> 00:42:52,610
Okay.

1052
00:42:52,610 --> 00:42:53,910
(You're giving us a present?)

1053
00:42:53,910 --> 00:42:54,910
I don't believe it yet.

1054
00:42:55,950 --> 00:42:58,780
(A real package of gifts appears right in front of them.)

1055
00:42:59,520 --> 00:43:00,520
A present?

1056
00:43:01,220 --> 00:43:02,520
(Glancing)

1057
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:04,520
No way. I don't believe you.

1058
00:43:04,520 --> 00:43:05,860
Why would you do this to us?

1059
00:43:06,090 --> 00:43:09,090
(Despite their words of suspicion, their hands are busy unwrapping.)

1060
00:43:10,060 --> 00:43:12,430
Goodness. What is it?

1061
00:43:13,330 --> 00:43:14,430
(This is no time to be messing around.)

1062
00:43:14,430 --> 00:43:16,130
(A mysterious T-shirt?)

1063
00:43:16,130 --> 00:43:17,570
"This is no time to be messing around."

1064
00:43:17,570 --> 00:43:18,570
"It's a war every single day."

1065
00:43:18,570 --> 00:43:20,740
(By Yum Jung Ah)

1066
00:43:21,100 --> 00:43:22,300
(Trying to figure out the situation)

1067
00:43:22,300 --> 00:43:24,840
(Why is my name on it?)

1068
00:43:25,110 --> 00:43:26,140
(Rustling)

1069
00:43:26,980 --> 00:43:28,940
"I'll do my best for our viewers."

1070
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:30,110
What's this?

1071
00:43:30,980 --> 00:43:33,480
(Okay, this is the kind of gift it is.)

1072
00:43:34,450 --> 00:43:35,720
"I'm the type of person who gets energized..."

1073
00:43:35,720 --> 00:43:38,950
"I'm the type of person who gets energized by working."

1074
00:43:39,320 --> 00:43:40,360
I love it.

1075
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:42,320
(Completely satisfied)

1076
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:43,330
Jung Ah.

1077
00:43:44,230 --> 00:43:46,360
"Is it hot? I'll just let myself sweat."

1078
00:43:46,700 --> 00:43:47,700
Did I say this?

1079
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:51,000
- Did I say this?
- Did I really say this?

1080
00:43:51,000 --> 00:43:52,000
(Let me think...)

1081
00:43:52,230 --> 00:43:53,740
Did I say something so positive?

1082
00:43:53,740 --> 00:43:55,170
Did I say something so positive?

1083
00:43:56,140 --> 00:43:57,170
You guys have changed.

1084
00:43:58,040 --> 00:44:01,180
(About 6 months ago when things were quite different)

1085
00:44:01,480 --> 00:44:04,610
(Back when they first met before filming)

1086
00:44:04,610 --> 00:44:05,650
I feel a lot of pressure.

1087
00:44:06,220 --> 00:44:08,180
I look forward to working with you.

1088
00:44:08,950 --> 00:44:11,320
(This is what the three siblings said back then.)

1089
00:44:11,590 --> 00:44:14,260
Is it hot? I'll just let myself sweat.

1090
00:44:15,260 --> 00:44:17,530
I'm the type of person who gets energized...

1091
00:44:17,530 --> 00:44:19,300
by working.

1092
00:44:19,530 --> 00:44:22,200
I'll do my best for our viewers.

1093
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:25,170
You don't know because...

1094
00:44:25,170 --> 00:44:26,500
you haven't been out in the field yet.

1095
00:44:26,500 --> 00:44:27,570
(Jung Ah saw the younger siblings get excited.)

1096
00:44:27,570 --> 00:44:28,800
This is no time...

1097
00:44:28,800 --> 00:44:30,070
- to be messing around.
- I understand.

1098
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:32,410
It's a war every single day.

1099
00:44:33,240 --> 00:44:34,280
(Buried deep in your hearts)

1100
00:44:34,280 --> 00:44:37,950
(We'll return their initial spirit.)

1101
00:44:39,720 --> 00:44:40,820
(This is no time to be messing around.)

1102
00:44:40,820 --> 00:44:41,920
(It's a war every single day.)

1103
00:44:43,320 --> 00:44:45,620
(I'll do my best for our viewers.)

1104
00:44:46,320 --> 00:44:49,190
(Is it hot? I'll just let myself sweat.)

1105
00:44:49,430 --> 00:44:54,230
(I'm the type of person who gets energized by working.)

1106
00:44:54,730 --> 00:44:56,200
This is your initial spirit.

1107
00:44:57,570 --> 00:44:59,270
My initial spirit hasn't changed.

1108
00:44:59,270 --> 00:45:00,800
- Dear viewers, - Sun Young hasn't changed.

1109
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:02,370
- my initial spirit hasn't changed.
- She's the only one.

1110
00:45:02,370 --> 00:45:03,370
Hers is the same.

1111
00:45:03,470 --> 00:45:04,540
Mine is the same.

1112
00:45:04,540 --> 00:45:05,610
(She preserved and even evolved her initial spirit.)

1113
00:45:05,810 --> 00:45:07,980
- I lost my initial spirit.
- I did too.

1114
00:45:08,140 --> 00:45:10,410
Is it hot? I'll just go inside and sleep.

1115
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:12,680
You need to stay under the air conditioner.

1116
00:45:12,880 --> 00:45:13,950
Thank you.

1117
00:45:14,680 --> 00:45:15,680
I like it.

1118
00:45:16,090 --> 00:45:19,720
Let's remember our initial spirit, wear these T-shirts,

1119
00:45:19,920 --> 00:45:21,760
and finish the journey on a high note.

1120
00:45:22,160 --> 00:45:23,230
What will we be doing?

1121
00:45:23,790 --> 00:45:26,130
- We're going to the sea.
- What?

1122
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:28,060
We're going to the sea.

1123
00:45:29,230 --> 00:45:30,330
- Really?
- At this time?

1124
00:45:30,870 --> 00:45:32,570
- Seriously?
- At this hour?

1125
00:45:33,170 --> 00:45:34,200
Are we going to the sea?

1126
00:45:34,840 --> 00:45:36,470
- We have to time it with the tides.
- For octopus?

1127
00:45:36,470 --> 00:45:37,470
- The tides?
- Octopus?

1128
00:45:37,740 --> 00:45:38,770
We're catching octopus.

1129
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:40,780
The sea? Okay.

1130
00:45:41,740 --> 00:45:42,850
I'll work hard.

1131
00:45:42,850 --> 00:45:44,780
(Let's take our original spirit and head to the sea.)

1132
00:45:45,080 --> 00:45:46,120
Does it show?

1133
00:45:46,120 --> 00:45:47,380
(Remove the bag)

1134
00:45:47,380 --> 00:45:48,680
It has to show.

1135
00:45:48,750 --> 00:45:51,150
(Protect the siblings' original spirit at all cost)

1136
00:45:51,920 --> 00:45:55,090
(Got their original spirit back, passion)

1137
00:45:56,060 --> 00:45:57,130
That's enough. It's hot.

1138
00:45:57,130 --> 00:45:58,330
(Get away from me.)

1139
00:45:58,330 --> 00:45:59,830
- Jung Ah.
- I knew she'd say that.

1140
00:46:00,460 --> 00:46:01,860
- I knew it.
- It was a close call.

1141
00:46:02,160 --> 00:46:03,270
(We stayed stuck together for long enough.)

1142
00:46:03,370 --> 00:46:06,370
- Let's go.
- Wait, before we go...

1143
00:46:07,170 --> 00:46:10,010
I got something for all of you.

1144
00:46:10,240 --> 00:46:11,240
What is it?

1145
00:46:12,010 --> 00:46:15,110
These gummy vitamins are convenient to take when you're busy.

1146
00:46:16,380 --> 00:46:18,910
I know about these. They're so good.

1147
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:21,420
(Popping one into her mouth)

1148
00:46:21,720 --> 00:46:23,850
We have to eat it and take care of our health.

1149
00:46:24,820 --> 00:46:25,990
(It's very tangy.)

1150
00:46:26,320 --> 00:46:28,120
They're delicious and packed with vitamins.

1151
00:46:28,120 --> 00:46:29,160
(Captain Yum also pops some vitamin into her mouth.)

1152
00:46:29,290 --> 00:46:30,430
It's delicious.

1153
00:46:31,890 --> 00:46:33,260
- It tastes like tangerines.
- How much vitamin content...

1154
00:46:33,660 --> 00:46:35,230
It's so convenient to take on the go.

1155
00:46:35,500 --> 00:46:37,870
It's easy to eat because it comes in a jelly form.

1156
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:40,440
Let's bring some with us and eat it whenever we get tired.

1157
00:46:41,200 --> 00:46:42,200
- It's good.
- It's tasty.

1158
00:46:42,300 --> 00:46:43,810
- It's like a dessert.
- I like this.

1159
00:46:44,040 --> 00:46:45,140
It's nice and tangy.

1160
00:46:45,840 --> 00:46:48,740
(Energy replenished)

1161
00:46:49,380 --> 00:46:52,150
- Is everyone ready?
- Okay, let's head out.

1162
00:46:52,150 --> 00:46:53,220
Let's go.

1163
00:46:53,480 --> 00:46:54,550
Let's get going.

1164
00:46:56,290 --> 00:46:59,150
- The mural looks so beautiful.
- I know.

1165
00:46:59,290 --> 00:47:00,460
My goodness.

1166
00:47:00,620 --> 00:47:02,620
What else could you possibly add? It's already packed.

1167
00:47:03,830 --> 00:47:06,960
Look at the whale. It's about to fly away.

1168
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:09,130
The whale looks like it's jumping.

1169
00:47:09,130 --> 00:47:10,200
- Isn't it amazing?
- Yes.

1170
00:47:10,600 --> 00:47:12,870
The whale, the yellow fish,

1171
00:47:12,870 --> 00:47:14,300
and the boat are huge.

1172
00:47:15,740 --> 00:47:17,210
I like it.

1173
00:47:17,370 --> 00:47:19,410
It looks so lovely.

1174
00:47:19,610 --> 00:47:22,110
We went through many hardships and challenges.

1175
00:47:22,280 --> 00:47:23,810
Now that it's done, I feel so proud of it.

1176
00:47:23,810 --> 00:47:24,810
(Pride level at maximum)

1177
00:47:24,810 --> 00:47:26,380
That's what makes me the proudest.

1178
00:47:26,380 --> 00:47:28,150
(The captain loves it too.)

1179
00:47:28,280 --> 00:47:31,420
Someone who watched the show might happen to visit Yeosu...

1180
00:47:31,750 --> 00:47:33,960
- and come by to see the mural.
- That's possible.

1181
00:47:33,960 --> 00:47:35,020
Right.

1182
00:47:35,020 --> 00:47:36,020
(Always thinking of our viewers)

1183
00:47:36,020 --> 00:47:39,330
Let's write "the siblings" and "Sang Hun" on the mural.

1184
00:47:39,460 --> 00:47:40,800
We definitely should.

1185
00:47:40,800 --> 00:47:42,700
(The four siblings look forward to seeing the finished piece.)

1186
00:47:43,000 --> 00:47:44,300
What kind of work will we be doing?

1187
00:47:44,300 --> 00:47:45,830
(By now, everyone's curious about today's workplace.)

1188
00:47:45,900 --> 00:47:47,200
(Curious)

1189
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:48,240
I wonder what we're doing.

1190
00:47:48,240 --> 00:47:50,110
What was written there again?

1191
00:47:50,610 --> 00:47:51,710
Hairtail.

1192
00:47:52,470 --> 00:47:54,280
I think it'll be octopus.

1193
00:47:54,710 --> 00:47:56,450
If we really catch octopus, does that mean we get to eat it?

1194
00:47:56,650 --> 00:47:57,980
- Octopus is delicious.
- It really is.

1195
00:47:58,910 --> 00:48:01,980
(Lost in happy thoughts, they arrive at the harbor.)

1196
00:48:03,950 --> 00:48:05,590
- All right.
- All right.

1197
00:48:05,990 --> 00:48:07,060
We can do it.

1198
00:48:07,560 --> 00:48:09,260
- We can do it.
- Hello, viewers.

1199
00:48:09,860 --> 00:48:11,030
We can do it.

1200
00:48:11,030 --> 00:48:13,000
- We'll give it our best shot.
- Yes.

1201
00:48:14,100 --> 00:48:16,900
(Getting ready to set sail)

1202
00:48:17,630 --> 00:48:18,870
(The siblings are determined for their last labor work.)

1203
00:48:18,870 --> 00:48:20,470
- All right!
- All right.

1204
00:48:22,100 --> 00:48:23,340
I can smell the sea.

1205
00:48:24,410 --> 00:48:26,540
I wonder what we're going to catch.

1206
00:48:27,180 --> 00:48:28,280
It's...

1207
00:48:28,710 --> 00:48:30,950
so hot that you can't even sit still.

1208
00:48:30,950 --> 00:48:33,080
(The Yeosu sun is still blazing hot.)

1209
00:48:33,550 --> 00:48:38,190
I can smell the sea. What are we going to catch?

1210
00:48:38,820 --> 00:48:40,420
Gosh, look at that. What?

1211
00:48:41,090 --> 00:48:43,230
The boat is really big.

1212
00:48:43,930 --> 00:48:45,460
(Different from anything we've seen before)

1213
00:48:45,460 --> 00:48:46,560
The boat is huge.

1214
00:48:46,560 --> 00:48:48,400
Is this the biggest boat we've ever been on?

1215
00:48:48,560 --> 00:48:49,870
It's very big.

1216
00:48:50,670 --> 00:48:52,770
- Is that a net?
- It's a net.

1217
00:48:52,770 --> 00:48:54,170
(A net that seems to stretch on forever?)

1218
00:48:54,400 --> 00:48:55,640
What are we going to catch?

1219
00:48:55,640 --> 00:48:56,810
(The closer they get, the more impressive the scale becomes.)

1220
00:48:56,810 --> 00:48:57,840
Hey.

1221
00:48:57,840 --> 00:48:58,870
(They arrive at the scene.)

1222
00:48:58,870 --> 00:48:59,980
- Hello.
- Hello.

1223
00:49:00,940 --> 00:49:03,510
(Even Jung Ah looks visibly nervous.)

1224
00:49:04,150 --> 00:49:05,210
I can't wait to find out.

1225
00:49:05,210 --> 00:49:06,820
(What will be their last labor work?)

1226
00:49:07,380 --> 00:49:10,390
The boat you'll be boarding today is...

1227
00:49:10,520 --> 00:49:14,190
a 24-ton set net fishing vessel.

1228
00:49:14,990 --> 00:49:17,660
(Today's work is set net fishing.)

1229
00:49:18,060 --> 00:49:20,500
- Jung Ah, you probably know...
- I do.

1230
00:49:20,500 --> 00:49:21,500
(The only one with previous set net fishing experience)

1231
00:49:22,060 --> 00:49:23,070
(It's the first time for the younger siblings.)

1232
00:49:23,070 --> 00:49:24,130
What's set net fishing?

1233
00:49:24,700 --> 00:49:26,300
With set net fishing,

1234
00:49:26,300 --> 00:49:29,000
you never know what type of fish you'll catch.

1235
00:49:29,870 --> 00:49:32,870
(Worthy of our last fresh delivery)

1236
00:49:33,480 --> 00:49:35,940
(A massive 24-ton vessel)

1237
00:49:37,280 --> 00:49:40,220
(In the pristine water of Yeosu)

1238
00:49:40,220 --> 00:49:42,420
(Set net fishing)

1239
00:49:42,780 --> 00:49:45,220
Set net fishing is a passive fishing method.

1240
00:49:45,220 --> 00:49:46,420
(Nets are set up along the fish's migration routes.)

1241
00:49:46,420 --> 00:49:49,090
The nets are left in place. That's where fishing takes place.

1242
00:49:49,090 --> 00:49:51,930
(The fish are caught once they enter the nets.)

1243
00:49:51,930 --> 00:49:54,160
As soon as we enter the fishing ground,

1244
00:49:54,330 --> 00:49:57,100
we slowly guide the fish toward the front.

1245
00:49:57,600 --> 00:50:00,070
At the end, we scoop them up with a landing net.

1246
00:50:00,270 --> 00:50:01,570
We pull them up.

1247
00:50:01,570 --> 00:50:03,040
(The fish are hauled aboard using a landing net.)

1248
00:50:04,140 --> 00:50:07,210
(Since the catch varies from day to day,)

1249
00:50:07,540 --> 00:50:12,150
(no one knows what kind of fish they'll catch today.)

1250
00:50:12,480 --> 00:50:14,880
In the summer, it could be Japanese Spanish mackerel,

1251
00:50:15,450 --> 00:50:16,450
silver pomfret,

1252
00:50:17,290 --> 00:50:18,290
or hairtail.

1253
00:50:18,290 --> 00:50:19,590
(Hairtail, greater amberjack)

1254
00:50:19,590 --> 00:50:21,520
(Eel, red seabream,)

1255
00:50:21,520 --> 00:50:23,430
(stingray, octopus)

1256
00:50:23,590 --> 00:50:26,430
We don't chase after the fish to catch different species.

1257
00:50:26,430 --> 00:50:29,130
When the season comes, the fish show up right on cue.

1258
00:50:30,970 --> 00:50:36,470
(What kind of fish will the siblings encounter today?)

1259
00:50:36,540 --> 00:50:38,940
- Okay.
- My gosh.

1260
00:50:38,940 --> 00:50:39,980
A random mix?

1261
00:50:40,710 --> 00:50:41,740
Okay.

1262
00:50:42,210 --> 00:50:43,450
That sounds good.

1263
00:50:44,150 --> 00:50:45,510
It will be fun.

1264
00:50:46,780 --> 00:50:48,920
- We don't know what we'll catch.
- Let's go.

1265
00:50:48,920 --> 00:50:49,990
Let's go.

1266
00:50:49,990 --> 00:50:51,190
(The boat for the siblings is waiting at the dock.)

1267
00:50:51,950 --> 00:50:54,090
(You Seok is the first to board.)

1268
00:50:54,090 --> 00:50:55,720
- Let me give you a hand.
- Like that?

1269
00:50:56,990 --> 00:50:58,690
(The siblings board in order.)

1270
00:50:58,690 --> 00:50:59,730
Gosh.

1271
00:51:00,300 --> 00:51:02,900
(Each of them steps aboard with determination.)

1272
00:51:02,900 --> 00:51:03,900
It's too high.

1273
00:51:04,400 --> 00:51:06,300
You can do it because you have long legs.

1274
00:51:07,100 --> 00:51:08,100
(All right)

1275
00:51:10,270 --> 00:51:11,310
Bye.

1276
00:51:11,570 --> 00:51:12,670
Goodbye.

1277
00:51:16,080 --> 00:51:17,310
Hello.

1278
00:51:17,310 --> 00:51:18,650
(The moment they get on board, the nerves kick in.)

1279
00:51:18,650 --> 00:51:20,220
- Hello.
- Hello.

1280
00:51:20,220 --> 00:51:22,220
- Welcome to the inferno.
- Hello.

1281
00:51:22,220 --> 00:51:23,950
(Welcome to the inferno.)

1282
00:51:23,950 --> 00:51:25,450
- What? Inferno?
- This is the inferno.

1283
00:51:25,450 --> 00:51:26,760
Yes. I'm glad that you came.

1284
00:51:26,760 --> 00:51:27,760
We're in trouble.

1285
00:51:27,760 --> 00:51:28,760
Why is it the inferno?

1286
00:51:28,990 --> 00:51:30,460
- The weather is hot.
- Is it the inferno?

1287
00:51:30,460 --> 00:51:31,590
It's the inferno.

1288
00:51:31,590 --> 00:51:32,730
(The only one who's experienced)

1289
00:51:32,890 --> 00:51:35,730
The weather is hot, so you'll have a tough time.

1290
00:51:35,730 --> 00:51:36,800
Okay.

1291
00:51:36,870 --> 00:51:37,930
We're in trouble.

1292
00:51:37,930 --> 00:51:39,100
(Everyone is nervous.)

1293
00:51:39,370 --> 00:51:40,900
Do you usually go out fishing when it's this hot?

1294
00:51:40,900 --> 00:51:42,400
- Yes, we usually do.
- Why?

1295
00:51:42,400 --> 00:51:43,970
You go out to sea even in this scorching sun?

1296
00:51:43,970 --> 00:51:45,470
We go out twice a day.

1297
00:51:45,470 --> 00:51:47,110
Once at dawn and once in the afternoon.

1298
00:51:47,110 --> 00:51:48,280
- Once in the afternoon?
- Yes.

1299
00:51:48,410 --> 00:51:50,050
- Shall we get going?
- Yes.

1300
00:51:50,050 --> 00:51:52,910
(Setting out to sea for fishing)

1301
00:51:55,350 --> 00:51:56,520
I'm so excited.

1302
00:51:56,790 --> 00:51:58,450
I love things like this.

1303
00:51:58,450 --> 00:51:59,450
(They're bursting with excitement for their biggest fishing trip yet.)

1304
00:51:59,450 --> 00:52:01,620
- I feel so good right now.
- Me too.

1305
00:52:02,820 --> 00:52:04,830
Gosh, this is exciting.

1306
00:52:05,360 --> 00:52:07,230
Although it'll be exhausting later.

1307
00:52:10,800 --> 00:52:12,700
The breeze makes it bearable.

1308
00:52:12,700 --> 00:52:13,970
Thank goodness for the wind.

1309
00:52:14,170 --> 00:52:16,570
- This is exciting.
- Look over there. It's so vast.

1310
00:52:16,640 --> 00:52:17,740
- Where?
- It's so vast.

1311
00:52:18,270 --> 00:52:19,270
- It's endless.
- Goodness.

1312
00:52:19,270 --> 00:52:20,440
(Savoring their last moments of leisure)

1313
00:52:20,440 --> 00:52:21,480
It looks magnificent.

1314
00:52:22,510 --> 00:52:26,280
(In the middle of the sea)

1315
00:52:27,420 --> 00:52:31,150
(The siblings' grand expedition is about to start.)

1316
00:52:32,590 --> 00:52:35,290
(Led by Captain Yum, the only one with experience)

1317
00:52:36,160 --> 00:52:37,430
(The rising star of the fishing world)

1318
00:52:37,430 --> 00:52:38,760
(An art major)

1319
00:52:39,630 --> 00:52:41,860
(And raised by the East Sea)

1320
00:52:42,100 --> 00:52:45,030
(Captain Kang from Gangneung)

1321
00:52:45,600 --> 00:52:47,170
(And...)

1322
00:52:47,640 --> 00:52:50,570
(the fish fanatic who takes work more seriously than anyone else)

1323
00:52:51,540 --> 00:52:52,640
(Their one and only goal)

1324
00:52:52,640 --> 00:52:55,640
(A boatload of fish)

1325
00:52:59,820 --> 00:53:03,950
(Doing their best to look cool)

1326
00:53:03,950 --> 00:53:06,390
(She tries not to laugh but fails.)

1327
00:53:06,860 --> 00:53:08,090
Don't we look determined?

1328
00:53:08,090 --> 00:53:09,120
Sure, you do.

1329
00:53:09,120 --> 00:53:10,590
(That's all that matters.)

1330
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:12,090
Please take a photo of us.

1331
00:53:12,430 --> 00:53:14,500
(They had no idea what was coming.)

1332
00:53:15,660 --> 00:53:17,430
(Last winter)

1333
00:53:17,430 --> 00:53:19,130
(At the freezing sea at minus 15°C)

1334
00:53:19,300 --> 00:53:21,740
(Taking on an extreme fishing challenge)

1335
00:53:22,040 --> 00:53:24,340
(The biggest set net fishing operation)

1336
00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:26,070
(And today)

1337
00:53:26,480 --> 00:53:28,740
(Under the blazing sun reaching 36°C)

1338
00:53:29,340 --> 00:53:32,180
(Cries of exhaustion ring out from every direction.)

1339
00:53:33,820 --> 00:53:34,950
(This is so hard.)

1340
00:53:35,180 --> 00:53:36,380
(There are too many.)

1341
00:53:36,750 --> 00:53:39,290
(Clenching his teeth)

1342
00:53:40,490 --> 00:53:42,290
(Be careful with your hands around the hairtail.)

1343
00:53:42,720 --> 00:53:43,960
(And...)

1344
00:53:43,960 --> 00:53:47,030
(it even brings optimistic Yoon Seo to tears.)

1345
00:53:47,600 --> 00:53:50,930
(An unprecedentedly massive fishing operation is coming.)

1346
00:53:53,339 --> 00:53:56,169
(Captain Yum is keeping a sharp eye on something.)

1347
00:53:56,339 --> 00:53:59,639
Do you see those wooden crates over there?

1348
00:53:59,839 --> 00:54:02,449
(Stacks of crates piled up where Captain Yum is pointing)

1349
00:54:02,709 --> 00:54:06,249
They'll probably put the fish in those crates by species.

1350
00:54:08,349 --> 00:54:10,359
(An instinct developed through experience)

1351
00:54:10,819 --> 00:54:13,389
(She figured out the task just by looking at the crates.)

1352
00:54:13,559 --> 00:54:15,829
Was the boat yesterday much smaller than this one?

1353
00:54:15,829 --> 00:54:17,429
- Yes.
- It was much smaller.

1354
00:54:17,699 --> 00:54:18,759
It was much smaller.

1355
00:54:19,099 --> 00:54:21,769
I never imagined riding such a big boat on the last day.

1356
00:54:22,429 --> 00:54:25,069
I kept wondering why we never went on a big boat.

1357
00:54:25,799 --> 00:54:27,909
I thought we weren't going to ride one this big.

1358
00:54:27,909 --> 00:54:28,939
But on the last day...

1359
00:54:30,209 --> 00:54:31,939
(After 25 minutes of sailing,)

1360
00:54:31,939 --> 00:54:33,879
(the boat finally reaches the fishing ground.)

1361
00:54:34,579 --> 00:54:36,279
I'm starting to see movements.

1362
00:54:36,279 --> 00:54:37,349
(The crew members emerge 1 by 1.)

1363
00:54:37,579 --> 00:54:39,879
(They move busily to get into position.)

1364
00:54:40,049 --> 00:54:42,289
- We've reached our fishing ground.
- Okay.

1365
00:54:42,289 --> 00:54:44,519
Once the crew members come out,

1366
00:54:44,519 --> 00:54:47,689
they'll start by operating the roller equipment.

1367
00:54:47,689 --> 00:54:50,229
It can be dangerous during the task, so we'll stay back.

1368
00:54:50,229 --> 00:54:52,429
- Okay.
- When I call you out,

1369
00:54:52,429 --> 00:54:54,769
- please help them pull up the net.
- Okay.

1370
00:54:56,669 --> 00:54:58,739
- Should we step back?
- Yes, please step back.

1371
00:54:58,739 --> 00:54:59,769
Jung Ah, come this way.

1372
00:55:00,269 --> 00:55:01,439
(The rolling done by the crew)

1373
00:55:01,439 --> 00:55:02,639
It's huge.

1374
00:55:04,539 --> 00:55:06,949
This machine works automatically.

1375
00:55:06,949 --> 00:55:10,079
It catches the next section of the line and pulls it.

1376
00:55:10,079 --> 00:55:11,119
(The roller is used to haul in the net from far out at sea.)

1377
00:55:11,549 --> 00:55:14,189
(When he winds the roller,)

1378
00:55:14,189 --> 00:55:17,589
(the net slowly begins to come in.)

1379
00:55:18,089 --> 00:55:19,719
(Only experienced workers handle it...)

1380
00:55:19,719 --> 00:55:21,389
(because there's a risk of being dragged into the sea.)

1381
00:55:22,659 --> 00:55:25,229
I'm so curious. I've never seen it before.

1382
00:55:26,869 --> 00:55:30,669
The net must be placed very deep in the ocean.

1383
00:55:31,039 --> 00:55:32,939
(Bursting with excitement)

1384
00:55:32,939 --> 00:55:33,969
I'm so nervous.

1385
00:55:34,809 --> 00:55:37,809
(With the freshly caught sea creatures coming aboard,)

1386
00:55:38,339 --> 00:55:41,649
(there's a whirlwind of activity on site.)

1387
00:55:42,079 --> 00:55:44,649
(The tension is contagious.)

1388
00:55:44,719 --> 00:55:49,319
Once they pull it up, the net will be packed with fish.

1389
00:55:50,059 --> 00:55:52,319
(Experienced Jung Ah is so nervous.)

1390
00:55:52,489 --> 00:55:53,629
That side is coming out.

1391
00:55:53,889 --> 00:55:55,459
- Where?
- The net.

1392
00:55:56,259 --> 00:55:57,899
All right. Pull it up.

1393
00:55:57,899 --> 00:55:59,199
(Suddenly, the crew members start working faster.)

1394
00:55:59,899 --> 00:56:03,469
(As the net rises, the fish finally start to appear.)

1395
00:56:03,599 --> 00:56:05,799
It's coming up. There's a hairtail.

1396
00:56:06,339 --> 00:56:07,739
(Where?)

1397
00:56:09,539 --> 00:56:10,639
- Gosh.
- Oh, my.

1398
00:56:11,339 --> 00:56:13,809
(Some of them are already making quite an impression.)

1399
00:56:14,449 --> 00:56:15,609
What type of fish is that?

1400
00:56:15,979 --> 00:56:17,779
- Look at them.
- Look at them.

1401
00:56:17,779 --> 00:56:19,379
- They came to eat.
- They're being pulled up.

1402
00:56:19,379 --> 00:56:22,819
(Even their silhouettes look extraordinary.)

1403
00:56:23,089 --> 00:56:24,159
(They're fascinated by what they're seeing.)

1404
00:56:24,159 --> 00:56:25,259
What type of fish is that?

1405
00:56:26,219 --> 00:56:28,559
- Please pull up the net right now.
- Okay.

1406
00:56:28,559 --> 00:56:30,029
Please help us even if it gets tough.

1407
00:56:30,029 --> 00:56:31,259
- Where's the net?
- What should we do?

1408
00:56:32,299 --> 00:56:33,399
It's heavy.

1409
00:56:34,269 --> 00:56:35,429
- Do we pull it?
- Yes.

1410
00:56:35,429 --> 00:56:37,139
My goodness.

1411
00:56:37,739 --> 00:56:39,439
Just make sure it doesn’t slip backward.

1412
00:56:39,739 --> 00:56:41,209
Gosh, wait a minute.

1413
00:56:41,209 --> 00:56:42,239
Grab it here.

1414
00:56:42,969 --> 00:56:44,939
- Slowly.
- Slowly.

1415
00:56:44,939 --> 00:56:46,539
- One. Slowly.
- One.

1416
00:56:46,539 --> 00:56:47,579
(Teamwork is crucial.)

1417
00:56:48,249 --> 00:56:50,579
(There's still a long way to go before the net comes up.)

1418
00:56:50,919 --> 00:56:52,549
(Take a deep breath and get ready)

1419
00:56:52,749 --> 00:56:55,089
(Everyone, pull together!)

1420
00:56:55,719 --> 00:56:57,459
(The net is ten times the size of a soccer field.)

1421
00:56:57,459 --> 00:56:58,889
Gosh, it's hard.

1422
00:56:59,059 --> 00:57:00,989
There are too many.

1423
00:57:01,659 --> 00:57:02,729
It's heavy.

1424
00:57:03,559 --> 00:57:06,429
(They can't let go of the net no matter how heavy it is.)

1425
00:57:07,799 --> 00:57:09,769
(The fish slowly begin to emerge.)

1426
00:57:09,769 --> 00:57:10,839
They're coming up.

1427
00:57:13,469 --> 00:57:14,539
It's so heavy.

1428
00:57:14,539 --> 00:57:16,409
(Now that they can see the fish, they find a burst of strength.)

1429
00:57:16,409 --> 00:57:17,809
Pull it slowly.

1430
00:57:19,739 --> 00:57:21,049
(Perfectly in sync)

1431
00:57:21,049 --> 00:57:24,479
With many people pulling together, the net comes up more easily.

1432
00:57:24,479 --> 00:57:27,489
(Working in sync makes hauling in the net a little easier.)

1433
00:57:28,889 --> 00:57:29,949
My gosh.

1434
00:57:29,949 --> 00:57:31,389
(Giving it all they've got)

1435
00:57:31,559 --> 00:57:32,559
(Heave-ho)

1436
00:57:33,689 --> 00:57:34,689
(Heave-ho)

1437
00:57:36,329 --> 00:57:38,599
(With everyone pulling together)

1438
00:57:38,599 --> 00:57:39,629
They're coming up.

1439
00:57:41,069 --> 00:57:42,069
Goodness.

1440
00:57:42,069 --> 00:57:43,469
(Hairtail start to emerge from the net.)

1441
00:57:44,799 --> 00:57:45,799
Goodness.

1442
00:57:46,169 --> 00:57:47,269
- Gosh.
- That's fascinating.

1443
00:57:47,269 --> 00:57:48,439
The hairtail are very silver.

1444
00:57:48,439 --> 00:57:49,439
(Flapping)

1445
00:57:49,439 --> 00:57:50,679
Pull it up slowly.

1446
00:57:51,179 --> 00:57:58,019
(Soon, the net is almost all the way up.)

1447
00:57:58,379 --> 00:58:00,449
(As they keep pulling, something yellow comes into view.)

1448
00:58:00,789 --> 00:58:03,389
- Is that a jellyfish?
- Yes, it's a Nomura's jellyfish.

1449
00:58:04,789 --> 00:58:06,929
- Do you throw the jellyfish away?
- Yes, we have to.

1450
00:58:08,629 --> 00:58:11,399
Changes in water temperature have been affecting the sea.

1451
00:58:11,599 --> 00:58:13,529
In the summer, jellyfish make it hard for us.

1452
00:58:13,799 --> 00:58:16,529
It's not just the fish. There are so many jellyfish.

1453
00:58:16,529 --> 00:58:17,799
(Due to the jellyfish, the catch has dropped significantly.)

1454
00:58:18,499 --> 00:58:22,309
(They witness a troubling reality of the ocean.)

1455
00:58:23,069 --> 00:58:29,379
(The jellyfish make the net even heavier.)

1456
00:58:31,549 --> 00:58:32,579
My goodness.

1457
00:58:32,579 --> 00:58:34,719
(Despite the jellyfish, they finish hauling in the net.)

1458
00:58:37,089 --> 00:58:39,189
- There are hairtail everywhere.
- My gosh.

1459
00:58:39,389 --> 00:58:40,459
They look beautiful.

1460
00:58:40,859 --> 00:58:41,959
My goodness.

1461
00:58:42,429 --> 00:58:46,059
(Swarming with fish)

1462
00:58:47,399 --> 00:58:51,439
(They're thrashing around with all their might.)

1463
00:58:52,969 --> 00:58:54,169
Can I get one too?

1464
00:58:54,169 --> 00:58:55,569
(They need to get those fish up onto the boat.)

1465
00:58:55,969 --> 00:58:58,939
(All kinds of fish are mixed inside the net.)

1466
00:58:59,939 --> 00:59:02,909
(The bigger fish are sorted out first...)

1467
00:59:02,909 --> 00:59:06,619
(with a landing net to avoid injuring them.)

1468
00:59:07,049 --> 00:59:09,089
Now we scoop them up with the landing net?

1469
00:59:09,089 --> 00:59:10,289
(Step 2. Landing Net)

1470
00:59:10,489 --> 00:59:12,089
Gosh, this is so long.

1471
00:59:12,089 --> 00:59:13,489
(Using a landing net that's much taller than a person)

1472
00:59:13,959 --> 00:59:15,889
(The job is to scoop the fish out of the net.)

1473
00:59:15,889 --> 00:59:16,899
(Grunting)

1474
00:59:17,329 --> 00:59:18,399
It's so heavy.

1475
00:59:20,129 --> 00:59:23,469
(The landing net is hard to control because it's long and heavy.)

1476
00:59:24,539 --> 00:59:26,699
How do I raise this?

1477
00:59:27,339 --> 00:59:29,509
(Even grown men struggle with it.)

1478
00:59:29,609 --> 00:59:31,409
(Exclaiming)

1479
00:59:32,079 --> 00:59:34,449
(Heave ho)

1480
00:59:34,649 --> 00:59:36,979
(She wipes off the sweat.)

1481
00:59:38,479 --> 00:59:40,819
(Jung Ah lifts the heavy landing net...)

1482
00:59:40,819 --> 00:59:43,959
(using the principle of leverage.)

1483
00:59:46,419 --> 00:59:48,759
(The landing net comes up.)

1484
00:59:49,229 --> 00:59:50,599
(She shakes it to drain off the water.)

1485
00:59:51,099 --> 00:59:54,229
(As someone experienced, her technique is on another level.)

1486
00:59:54,729 --> 00:59:55,929
Please bring it to this side.

1487
00:59:55,929 --> 00:59:58,099
(Gathering the fish in one spot before sorting)

1488
00:59:58,969 --> 01:00:01,609
(Carefully maneuvering the long landing net)

1489
01:00:03,069 --> 01:00:06,379
(They're finally aboard.)

1490
01:00:08,079 --> 01:00:09,109
(The fish are doing the twist.)

1491
01:00:09,109 --> 01:00:10,379
What type of fish is this?

1492
01:00:10,679 --> 01:00:11,749
It's greater amberjack.

1493
01:00:11,749 --> 01:00:14,089
(They can grow up to 2m long.)

1494
01:00:14,949 --> 01:00:16,189
(The younger ones are working hard with their nets.)

1495
01:00:16,189 --> 01:00:17,289
Can I get one too?

1496
01:00:17,289 --> 01:00:19,189
(The younger ones are working hard with their nets.)

1497
01:00:19,819 --> 01:00:22,289
(Under the scorching Yeosu sun)

1498
01:00:23,059 --> 01:00:25,199
(Their passion for the landing net never stops.)

1499
01:00:25,199 --> 01:00:26,199
My gosh.

1500
01:00:27,599 --> 01:00:30,129
(And...)

1501
01:00:30,799 --> 01:00:32,299
(Laughing joyfully)

1502
01:00:32,439 --> 01:00:33,439
(Guys, let's go.)

1503
01:00:33,439 --> 01:00:34,469
Let's go.

1504
01:00:34,809 --> 01:00:36,639
Guys, let's go.

1505
01:00:36,639 --> 01:00:38,979
(One of them is particularly excited.)

1506
01:00:39,239 --> 01:00:40,679
(Fish fanatic, Kim Sun Young)

1507
01:00:40,679 --> 01:00:42,409
Let's go.

1508
01:00:42,409 --> 01:00:44,579
(Track record: Wild eels, gizzard shads, and countless other fish)

1509
01:00:45,319 --> 01:00:46,379
Be careful.

1510
01:00:46,379 --> 01:00:47,689
(The fish fight back, thrashing wildly.)

1511
01:00:48,219 --> 01:00:50,119
(She overpowers them with strength.)

1512
01:00:50,119 --> 01:00:51,289
They're also...

1513
01:00:51,789 --> 01:00:54,359
Pull little by little. Be careful behind you.

1514
01:00:54,359 --> 01:00:55,389
I see.

1515
01:00:55,629 --> 01:00:56,659
This is fascinating.

1516
01:00:57,799 --> 01:00:59,659
(The feeling is thrilling.)

1517
01:00:59,659 --> 01:01:00,799
Be careful.

1518
01:01:00,799 --> 01:01:03,129
(Flapping)

1519
01:01:04,839 --> 01:01:09,239
(While Sun Young's dopamine levels are soaring)

1520
01:01:09,669 --> 01:01:10,839
It's an octopus.

1521
01:01:11,609 --> 01:01:12,639
An octopus.

1522
01:01:13,309 --> 01:01:15,149
It's an octopus.

1523
01:01:15,149 --> 01:01:16,409
- It's an octopus.
- Is there an octopus?

1524
01:01:16,549 --> 01:01:17,919
- There's an octopus.
- Octopus.

1525
01:01:17,919 --> 01:01:19,079
(An octopus shows its presence among the fish.)

1526
01:01:19,949 --> 01:01:22,619
(Hello, I'm an octopus.)

1527
01:01:25,689 --> 01:01:27,659
Octopus, come here.

1528
01:01:27,659 --> 01:01:29,289
(Yoon Seo is ready to hunt down the octopus.)

1529
01:01:30,159 --> 01:01:32,329
(Teto Yoon Seo versus Octopus)

1530
01:01:33,059 --> 01:01:34,169
No, octopus.

1531
01:01:34,169 --> 01:01:35,399
(The octopus hides and refuses to give in.)

1532
01:01:35,799 --> 01:01:37,569
- It's an octopus.
- Octopus.

1533
01:01:37,569 --> 01:01:39,299
- Octopus.
- She caught the octopus.

1534
01:01:39,299 --> 01:01:42,409
(The octopus enters.)

1535
01:01:42,909 --> 01:01:45,109
(It's an octopus.)

1536
01:01:45,409 --> 01:01:47,709
(All that's left is to haul it up.)

1537
